  "articleBody": "While cosmetic kitchen refreshes are straightforward, a kitchen addition involves major structural and systems modifications that call for hands-on general contracting.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- Removing exterior or load-bearing walls: Modifying structural framing requires engineered headers and proper temporary shoring to protect your home's stability.\n- Expanding your home's foundation or roofline: Tying a new bump-out into an existing roof and foundation demands precise weatherproofing and framing expertise.\n- Relocating main gas and plumbing lines: Gas piping and sink drains require licensed trade coordination, correct venting, and strict code compliance.\n- Upgrading main electrical panels: Adding high-draw ovens, microwaves, and lighting circuits often demands dedicated breakers and trade permits.\n- Preparing for municipal building inspections: Municipalities require staged rough-in inspections before any insulation or drywall work can proceed.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your project involves framing out new exterior space, coordinating specialized trades, and managing permits, working with an experienced builder protects your investment.\n\nReach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to discuss your kitchen addition plans and schedule an on-site consultation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
